Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: qcom-ipcc: mask summary IRQ in SM-X710 suspend too

ipcc-mask-summary-during-suspend-gts9u.patch drops IRQF_NO_SUSPEND from the
IPCC summary interrupt on the SM-X910 only, because ADSP SMP2P traffic made
that board's firmware return from PSCI SYSTEM_SUSPEND at once.  The SM-X710
(gts9wifi) runs the same SoC and Samsung firmware stack, and its one deep
suspend that reached PSCI with a working ADSP also returned within a second
without a wake IRQ.

Extend the board gate.  For deep suspend this is the Ultra fix.  For
suspend-to-idle it is not required -- the unmasked IRQ only wakes the CPUs,
and s2idle goes back to idle when no wakeup event was reported -- but it
keeps both modes identical: DSP messages stay latched in IPCC and are
handled after resume.  Other Qualcomm boards keep the upstream flag.

Applies on top of ipcc-mask-summary-during-suspend-gts9u.patch.

--- a/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
@@ -325,8 +325,15 @@ static int qcom_ipcc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_mbox;
 
-	/* Mask IPCC DSP traffic during SM-X910 system suspend. */
-	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,gts9uwifi"))
+	/*
+	 * Mask IPCC DSP traffic during SM-X910 system suspend.  The SM-X710
+	 * runs the same Samsung firmware, and one of its deep suspends also
+	 * came back at once without the power-key wake.  In suspend-to-idle
+	 * the mask only leaves DSP messages for resume, as in deep suspend,
+	 * instead of waking the CPUs for each one.
+	 */
+	if (!of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,gts9uwifi") &&
+	    !of_machine_is_compatible("samsung,gts9wifi"))
 		irqflags |= IRQF_NO_SUSPEND;
 
 	ret = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, ipcc->irq, qcom_ipcc_irq_fn,
